The shopkeeper dada nods.
He takes the small shirt back.
He gives me another shirt.
He says, 'Madam, this is bigger than this one.'
I take that new shirt in my hand.
There is a big mirror near the wall of the shop.
I step in front of that mirror.
I put that new shirt on right over my t-shirt.
I look in the mirror and button the shirt.
This new shirt is bigger than the old shirt.
The shoulders of this shirt are a bit wider than yesterday's shirt.
I move my arms to check.
I feel comfortable now.
Dada asks me, 'Madam, is the size okay?'
I nod to him.
I say, 'Yes, this shirt is much better than the previous shirt.'
This bigger shirt fits me perfectly.
